Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Did You Tape The Welder's Glass To The Chimney?
- Story & Context: When the backup diesel generator blew out behind the tilt-a-whirl at the Black Fork Fairgrounds, Hester Vance hauled an eighty-pound shime-daiko up the grease-slick ladder of the municipal water tower while the umbra raced across the cornfields at supersonic speed. Amateur astronomers in soot-stained parkas tripped over folding lawn chairs on the tar-paper rooftop below, clutching cardboard pinhole cameras as Hester’s banjo strings slashed through the frigid midday dark with the smell of clove cigarettes and scorched zinc. Before the crowd could flee the supernatural chill, the drums slammed down like an artillery barrage, her throat tearing through the megaphone hook: "Climb the rungs before the black coin drops!"
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: Album art shot from a low angle on an industrial rooftop, showing a rusted brick chimney taped with dark green welder's glass lenses, pointing toward a pitch-black eclipsed sun. Discarded lawn chairs, tangled mic leads, and flying wooden drumsticks are frozen mid-air against an eerie 2000s digital green-tinted sky, grainy and surreal.

Track 2: Rusty Downspouts Drink The Corona
- Story & Context: Perched over the parapet of a four-story boardinghouse in Cairo, Illinois, bassist Jude Mercer held a live microphone inside a vibrating copper downspout while Kenji Sato battered the wood-rimmed taiko until his palms bled onto the birch bachi. Jude had skipped bail on a grand larceny warrant three counties east just to meet the carnival train before totality, his fingers trembling across a flanged four-string neck as condensation from the sudden temperature drop soaked his thrift-store velvet frock coat. Amateur telescopes rattled around them on the tin decking as Jude whispered his confession into the howling wind, the chorus cutting across the sky: "You left your silver on the altar, but I needed the brass."
