Track 3: Gallow-Hollow Kurayami Reel
- Story & Context: On the rooftop of the abandoned St. Jude Sanatorium, the troupe struck up their final, frantic reel just as the moon began to slide away, daring the returning sunlight to blind the dozens of rooftop watchers whose smoked-glass viewing panes vibrated from the sheer acoustic displacement of the taiko shells. A local deputy tried to climb the rusted fire escape to cut the carnival's bootlegged power, but the stampede of runaway banjo arpeggios and thunderous skin-strikes knocked the ladder loose with a scream of sheared rivets. As the blistering diamond-ring flare exploded across the horizon, blinding three watchers who dropped their viewfinders into the street below, Hester screamed the legend into the feedback: "The day came back with empty pockets, but the dark belongs to us."
